          "text": "filename: docs/rename-photos.md\n```markdown\n# How to Rename a Folder of Holiday Photos with a Bash Loop\n\nThis guide shows how to automate the renaming of a folder of holiday photos using a bash loop. This is useful for organizing photos by date, making them easier to find, or preparing them for upload. The process involves iterating over files and applying a naming convention using shell scripting.\n\n## Example One: Date Prefix\nThis example adds a date prefix to each photo file in the format YYYY-MM-DD. The script assumes the files are in a folder named \"holiday_photos\".\n\n```bash\nfor file in holiday_photos/*; do\n    if [[ -f \"$file\" ]]; then\n        filename=$(basename \"$file\")\n        date_prefix=$(date -d \"2023-12-25\" +%Y-%m-%d)\n        new_name=\"${date_prefix}_${filename}\"\n        mv \"$file\" \"$new_name\"\n    fi\ndone\n```\n\n## Example Two: Lowercase Names\nThis example converts all file names to lowercase to ensure consistency and avoid case-sensitive issues in file systems.\n\n```bash\nfor file in holiday_photos/*; do\n    if [[ -f \"$file\" ]]; then\n        filename=$(basename \"$file\")\n        new_name=$(echo \"$filename\" | tr '[:upper:]' '[:lower:]')\n        mv \"$file\" \"$new_name\"\n    fi\ndone\n```\n\n## Example Three: Number the Files\nThis example renames files sequentially with a number prefix, useful for creating a clean, ordered list of photos.\n\n```bash\ni=1\nfor file in holiday_photos/*; do\n    if [[ -f \"$file\" ]]; then\n        filename=$(basename \"$file\")\n        new_name=\"photo_${i}_${filename}\"\n        mv \"$file\" \"$new_name\"\n        i=$((i + 1))\n    fi\ndone\n```\n\nWrap Up: This bash script efficiently organizes holiday photos using automation, improves file naming consistency, and saves time when managing large photo collections. It's simple to adapt, reliable for daily use, and ensures files are properly renamed with clear, predictable patterns.\n```",
